-- #2246 regression lock, FALSE-POSITIVE direction.  A clean MULTI-MODULE project
-- whose `main` is a plain Unit value must report ZERO diagnostics through
-- `check --json` (the `analyzeProject` route).
--
-- Until #2246 this golden was impossible: S-3 (#2234) deleted the extra
-- `elaborateModules` that used to populate `mainSchemeRef` for `checkJsonFile`'s
-- multi-module arm, and nothing on the `analyzeProject` → `typecheckPass` →
-- `checkModulesDiags` chain replaced it.  In a fresh process the ref is `None`,
-- `mainTypeIsUnit ()` answers False on `None`, and W-MAIN-SHAPE fired here — a
-- false positive on every `check --json` / MCP `medaka_check` of a multi-module
-- project with a perfectly good Unit main.
--
-- ⚠️ MULTI-MODULE ON PURPOSE: the single-module arm has always had a producer
-- (`analyzeLocatedG`), so a single-file version of this fixture is green either
-- way and proves nothing.
import lib.{bump}

main = println (bump 1)
